  "question": {
    "text": "A light string passing over a smooth light pulley connects two blocks of masses $\\mathrm{m}_1$ and $\\mathrm{m}_2$ (where $m_2 \\gt m_1$). If the acceleration of the system is $\\frac{\\mathrm{g}}{\\sqrt{2}}$, then the ratio of the masses $\\frac{m_1}{m_2}$ is:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "VYTEg",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-1}{\\sqrt{2}+1}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "Llr7i",
      "text": "$\\frac{1+\\sqrt{5}}{\\sqrt{5}-1}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "5e3pw",
      "text": "$\\frac{1+\\sqrt{5}}{\\sqrt{2}-1}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "O2ymy",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\sqrt{3}+1}{\\sqrt{2}-1}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Acceleration is given as:\n$a=\\left(\\frac{m_2-m_1}{m_1+m_2}\\right) g$\n$\\Rightarrow \\frac{\\mathrm{g}}{\\sqrt{2}}=\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{m}_2-\\mathrm{m}_1}{\\mathrm{~m}_1+\\mathrm{m}_2}\\right) \\mathrm{g}$\n$\\Rightarrow \\sqrt{2}\\left(m_2-m_1\\right)=m_1+m_2$\n$\\Rightarrow \\frac{\\mathrm{m}_1}{\\mathrm{~m}_2}=\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-1}{\\sqrt{2}+1}\\right)$",
    "image": null
  },
